.TH std::stoppable_token 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::stoppable_token \- std::stoppable_token

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <stop_token>
template< class Token >

concept stoppable_token =
requires (const Token tok) {
typename /*check-type-alias-exists*/<Token::template callback_type>;
{ tok.stop_requested() } noexcept -> std::same_as<bool>;              (since C++26)
{ tok.stop_possible() } noexcept -> std::same_as<bool>;
{ Token(tok) } noexcept; // see implicit expression variations
} &&
std::copyable<Token> &&

std::equality_comparable<Token>;
Helper templates
template< template<class> class >                                     (exposition only*)
struct /*check-type-alias-exists*/; // not defined

The concept stoppable_token<Token> specifies the basic interface of a stop token that is
copyable and equality_comparable and allows polling to see if the stop request is possible
and whether the request has been made.

